{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On the driver's own trace, his stationary in-geofence dwell at the pickup pin is 195 seconds. The free waiting period in force for this trip is 300 seconds, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec as POL-NS-01(c) directs and not the 180-second default. The shortfall is 105 seconds. POL-NS-06 makes the cancellation fee non-chargeable on that shortfall alone - whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she replied to any message - so the $4.00 charged must be refunded in full.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00203", "EV-TRIP-00203", "EV-FARE-00203"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 is deliberately conjunctive and limb (c) is broken. Limb (c) demands that the driver held position inside the geofence for a continuous dwell of at least the free waiting period in force; the measured run is 195 seconds against the 300 seconds carried by trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec for this STANDARD pickup. The rider wins by breaking a single limb, and the break is on the driver's own telemetry, not on any inference.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00203", "EV-TRIP-00203"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (d) of POL-NS-01 fails independently. It requires the termination to fall at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed. Measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 19:41:20, the 300-second period would have run out at about 19:46:20; the driver cancelled at 19:44:40, roughly 100 seconds early, and stamped the trip RIDER_NO_SHOW. A rider cannot be recorded as a no-show at a moment when the waiting period she paid for had not yet expired; the RIDER_NO_SHOW code is mis-selected and the fee is not chargeable on limb (d) either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00203", "EV-TRIP-00203"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortfall cannot be cured by accumulation under POL-NS-06(i). The trace shows a single in-geofence interval - run_count 1, the run from 19:41:20 to 19:44:35 - so there is no second interval to add. And limb (i) is unavailable on its own terms: EV-ADVIS-00203-01, the traffic advisory, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and a MISSING advisory makes limb (i) unavailable, so no KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT advisory can be asserted to extend the clock. Even doubling 195 seconds would not reach the 300-second minimum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00203", "EV-ADVIS-00203-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider was not an absent rider. Her own device track carries 60 qualifying fixes placing her between 36.4 m and 51.6 m of the pickup pin - inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius - continuously across the waiting window, and she messaged the driver at 19:42:50 to say she was coming down. Any reading of the record as a rider who failed to appear is contradicted by the rider's track; the charge fails on the driver's clock in any event. For transparency: EV-CHAT-00203 is impaired at weight_multiplier 0.85 with issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY (MSG-00203-002 is contestable between 'on my way' and 'already here'); I do not rest the refund on it, and the presence figures come from EV-GPS-00203, which the pre-pass assessed COMPLETE at weight 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00203", "EV-TRIP-00203", "EV-CHAT-00203"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No driver compensation can be paid on this record, and the refund is the whole contested sum. POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not; POL-NS-06 states that where cumulative dwell falls short of the minimum the full refund stands and no driver compensation is payable. The ledger confirms the fee_charged of 4.00 with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so on a FULL_REFUND the rider recovers the entire $4.00 and nothing is left standing against her.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00203", "EV-GPS-00203", "EV-DPROF-00203"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is engaged, so this should be decided on the arithmetic rather than sent to human review. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 limb (d) requires; rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, so limb (c) cannot fire; and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip because driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 - below the 4 of the first limb - and 2 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 131 is 0.015, below the 0.08 second limb, so both limbs fail and no compensation is withheld on that ground either. The deciding facts rest on artifacts at weight 1.0, above the 0.70 floor of POL-GEN-02 and POL-NS-09(a).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00203", "EV-DPROF-00203", "EV-GPS-00203"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The one impaired artifact in the bundle does not cap confidence or force escalation. EV-CHAT-00203 sits at weight_multiplier 0.85 with issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, and that impairment is schema-level only: it meets no limb (a) to (d) of POL-NS-08. There is no clock-skew tag on either EV-TRIP-00203 or EV-GPS-00203 (both COMPLETE, no issues); the trace reports gaps of [] and max_gap_sec 0.0 with 60 fixes across the window, so there is no gap over 120 seconds; the log holds 3 messages, matching trip_record.chat_message_count of 3; and the 4.00 cancellation line reconciles with the platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of 4.00, so POL-NS-08(d) is satisfied. Under POL-GEN-02 the chat is down-weighted in confidence when used, and I have not used it as the ground of the refund; it does not engage POL-NS-09(e).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00203", "EV-GPS-00203", "EV-FARE-00203", "EV-TRIP-00203"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.difference",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver — this ruling was made without human review and is provisional.\n\nRider, your $4.00 cancellation fee is returned in full. Driver, the fee does not stand and no compensation is payable to you.\n\nArrival was genuine, so the case turns on the clock. EV-GPS-00203 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius with 21 qualifying fixes at 5–11 m accuracy from 19:41:20, ahead of the 19:41:35 'arrived' event in EV-TRIP-00203; POL-NS-02 is satisfied and POL-NS-01 limb (b) holds. But POL-NS-01 is conjunctive and the remaining limbs break on the driver's own telemetry. The free waiting period in force is 300 seconds, read from EV-TRIP-00203 platform_policy.free_wait_sec as POL-NS-01(c) directs — not the 180-second fee_schedule default, and the same 5 minutes the app showed the rider. Limb (c) runs the clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix (19:41:20, not the 19:41:35 tap); EV-GPS-00203 shows one continuous run of 195 seconds ending 19:44:35 — a shortfall of 105 seconds. Limb (d) fails too: the driver terminated at 19:44:40, before the 300-second period would have elapsed at about 19:46:20. POL-NS-06 makes the fee non-chargeable on that shortfall alone, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she replied.\n\nThe shortfall cannot be cured. POL-NS-06(i) sums separate in-geofence intervals only with a qualifying traffic advisory, and there is one interval (run_count 1) and no advisory: EV-ADVIS-00203-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), so limb (i) is unavailable on its own terms, and even a second interval of the same length would not reach 300 seconds. POL-NS-05 does not apply: at the arrival marker the driver was stationary (0.0 km/h) and inside the radius, so the marker is genuine and no false-arrival record is made. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider here: the driver replied at 19:44:31, 101 seconds after the rider's 19:42:50 message, inside the 120-second window, so the clause does not run — the refund rests on the waiting-period arithmetic, not on the chat. The rider's own track (60 fixes, 36.4–51.6 m, inside the 100 m STANDARD radius) corroborates that she was present and coming down, but the refund does not depend on it.\n\nNo driver compensation. POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and POL-NS-06 states that no compensation is payable on a shortfall. EV-FARE-00203 confirms $4.00 charged, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the whole $4.00 is returned and $0.00 is paid to the driver.\n\nEvidence weight. EV-CHAT-00203 is impaired at weight 0.85 with issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY on MSG-00203-002; the finding does not rest on it and the presence figures come from EV-GPS-00203, assessed COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so the discount does not change the outcome. EV-ADVIS-00203-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and can carry no fact; its absence is itself what makes POL-NS-06(i) unavailable. The deciding facts — the 195-second dwell (EV-GPS-00203), the 300-second free wait and the 19:44:40 termination (EV-TRIP-00203) and the $4.00 charged (EV-FARE-00203) — all rest on artifacts at weight 1.0.\n\nNo escalation under POL-NS-09. The counterparty-dispute counters are 0; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (below 3); the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check fails both limbs (no_show_terminations_30d 2, below 4, and 2/131 = 0.015, below 0.08); and the sole deciding evidence is not impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d). Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nNo referral. RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the three codes POL-NS-01 limb (d) recognises; the driver-education referral for a mis-selected reason code attaches where a driver records a non-qualifying code such as DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE while actually inside the radius, which is not this case. The cancellation was premature, but the code was not outside limb (d)'s list, so no referral is recorded.\n\nThe monetary effect, $4.00, is below the $8.00 POL-GEN-05 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes on issue; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "I do not argue the fee above the record. The driver's continuous in-geofence hold was 195 seconds (19:41:20 to 19:44:35), 105 seconds short of the 300-second free waiting period in force on this trip from platform_policy.free_wait_sec, and POL-NS-06 limb (i) cannot make up the difference because the trace contains a single in-geofence interval and the only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00203-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0. On the strict-liability terms of POL-NS-06 the fee is not chargeable, and because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full POL-NS-07 gives the driver no compensation: the driver's claim to the $4.00 cannot be sustained on this evidence.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00203-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
