    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the $4.00 no-show cancellation fee does not stand, and the full $4.00 is refunded to the rider.\n\nWhy: the fee is chargeable only if the driver held position inside the pickup geofence for the whole free waiting period in force. On this trip that period is 300 seconds — read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec (EV-TRIP-00203, weight 1.0), not the 180-second default. The driver's own trace (EV-GPS-00203, weight 1.0) shows one continuous stationary hold inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 19:41:20 to 19:44:35: 195 seconds. The shortfall is 105 seconds. Under POL-NS-06 a shortfall makes the fee non-chargeable and it is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she replied. POL-NS-01 limb (c) fails for the same reason, and limb (d) fails independently: the 300-second wait would have run out at about 19:46:20, but the trip was cancelled at 19:44:40. The driver's RIDER_NO_SHOW code is one limb (d) recognises, but a no-show cannot be stamped before the waiting period has elapsed — so that part of the driver's case is rejected on the timing, not on the code. The shortfall cannot be cured under POL-NS-06(i): the trace shows a single in-geofence interval (run_count 1), so there is no second interval to add, and the only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00203-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), which makes limb (i) unavailable on its own terms.\n\nThe driver did genuinely arrive — 21 qualifying fixes at 5–11 m accuracy, the first at 19:41:20, with the BUTTON arrival marker at 19:41:35 not false — so POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-05 are satisfied and no false-arrival referral is recorded. But arrival alone does not make the fee chargeable when the waiting period was not served.\n\nNo driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not, and POL-NS-06 itself says the full refund stands with no compensation where the dwell falls short. The anti-farming check does not trip either (no_show_terminations_30d 2, below 4; 2 ÷ 131 = 0.015, below 0.08).\n\nNothing here escalates. The deciding facts — the 195-second dwell and the 300-second period in force — rest on EV-GPS-00203 and EV-TRIP-00203 at weight 1.0, so POL-NS-09(e) is not engaged; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence (POL-NS-09(b)); there are no same-party repeat disputes (0 and 0, POL-NS-09(c)); and no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below 3 (POL-NS-09(d)). EV-CHAT-00203 is impaired at weight_multiplier 0.85 for LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY and I name it as POL-GEN-02(3) requires, but this decision does not rest on it — the shortfall is arithmetic on the driver's own trace and survives the discount. The rider's own track places her 36.4–51.6 m from the pin (inside the 100 m STANDARD radius) and she messaged at 19:42:50; the driver replied at 19:44:31, inside the 120-second window, so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her on that path — but none of that decides the case, which turns on the waiting period alone.\n\nThe $4.00 monetary effect is below the POL-GEN-05 threshold of $8.00, so the refund executes automatically on issue. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "I do not argue the fee above the record. The driver's continuous in-geofence hold was 195 seconds (19:41:20 to 19:44:35), 105 seconds short of the 300-second free waiting period in force on this trip from platform_policy.free_wait_sec, and POL-NS-06 limb (i) cannot make up the difference because the trace contains a single in-geofence interval and the only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00203-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0. On the strict-liability terms of POL-NS-06 the fee is not chargeable, and because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full POL-NS-07 gives the driver no compensation: the driver's claim to the $4.00 cannot be sustained on this evidence.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00203-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
